    confirmed_exits: { cell: "K", fc: "K", ev: "NEISO-RC-R R1+Phase B (2026-08-31, FINDING-capx-neiso-rc-phase0 §10): registry completed (Mystic 8/9 rmr_end via 165 FERC ¶ 61,267; Potter/Yarmouth/Middletown/Waters River from the retrieved tracker, sha256 35075432…; CAR two-regime bar) and MEASURED in the rcrepair T1-X treatment vs the capxd14 control — 1,464 MW of the exit wave moved economic→confirmed (Mystic 706.7 MW derate 2024 + 706.7 drop 2025 + Potter 50.5), level ≈ unchanged (3.635 vs 3.563 GW; confirmed exits displace the floor-budgeted economic wave ≈1:1), Middletown exits economically 2024 ahead of its 2027 instrument (the min(economic, confirmed) ceiling working). The confirmed_derates half of a binned-plant exit is visible only through the R3(iii) scorer read." },
    economic_retirement_screen: { cell: "R", fc: "R", ev: "FFR-3A-2 (docs/handoffs/ffr-3a2-battery-close-2026-08-03.md §3.6 — run neiso-2021-2025-ffr3a2: refreshed but NOT ATTRIBUTED. retire.total 9.325→8.221, unit_recall PASS→FAIL; three candidate causes (entry_lookahead_reprice, D-1, D-2) plus the cache epoch, one measurement, no control arm); FFR-3A-3 (docs/handoffs/ffr-3a3-battery-close-2026-08-04.md §2.2/§5 — run neiso-2021-2025-realized-ffr3a3 RE-MEASURES THAT SAME LEG post-fix at 941f4983: retire.total_gw 8.221→7.585 vs 0.951 actual (closer, still ~8x), recall and false_retire FAIL unchanged. STILL NOT ATTRIBUTED — no control arm here either, so the same three candidate causes stand. What the leg DOES establish is an internal check on the re-measurement itself: EVERY additions band is BYTE-IDENTICAL across the fix (wind 1.0, solar 1.028, gas_ct 0.0, storage 0.0) while the retirement level moves, which is exactly the signature an exit-screen-only change must have. CELL UNCHANGED, determination UNMOVED (HOLD))" },
    capacity_market_clearing: { cell: "K", fc: "K", ev: "ff-2c; FFR-2E §3.1 (neiso-2021-2025-{shipped,fixed}-ffr2e: 10.465 vs 0.000 GW; shipped recall 1.000 vs fixed 0.000). NEISO-RC-R R2 (2026-08-31, FINDING-capx-neiso-rc-phase0 §10): the FCA curve RE-DERIVED from published MRI-era auction evidence (each vintage passes through its own auction's measured clearing point; zero-cross = FCA 13's published tail zero 1.0582, replacing the linear FCA-11 geometry's 1.083) — REFUTES the Phase-0 premise that the old curve underpaid at surplus: the measured curve pays LESS in (1.0, 1.06] and zeroes earlier. Phase B A/B (rcrepair vs capxd14, config-identical cache key): NEAR-INERT at the model's long positions (2024 screen position 1.295 → capacity leg $0 under both curves; the 2025 coal reversal at position 1.034 survives the less generous curve — reserve uplift ~$205/kW-yr dominates its $34 capacity leg). The R2 lever is SPENT for the composition miss; the outstanding object is the model's LONG position itself (1.295 vs the real market's ~1.03-1.05 — at real positions the re-derived curve pays $25-43/kW-yr, so the degenerate bar is a POSITION artifact, finding §10.4 item 2)." },
