    ccs_retrofit_capex_co2_scaling: { cell: ".", fc: "K", ev: "ARMED AS THE DEFAULT POSTURE 2026-09-05 by OWNER RULING Q42 (director sitting r#37), executed by capx D60 -- the ScenarioConfig default flips False -> True for ALL SIX ISOs, declared in _CACHE_KEY_OPTIONAL_FIELD_DEFAULT_FLIPS with the frozen drop value left at False ((b'-1), the D44 pattern); pins advance 4c6b03ae098b6e3e -> e5ecd4105ada3e58 (backcast 8211c72bb1960adc -> 6a2845e50951394e) and an explicit False still holds the pre-flip keys. It is a POSTURE, not a transfer (rule 25 intact): no ISO's fitted number is carried -- the island is sized against captured_ref 0.32319 t/MWh, the SAME reference host new_entry._emerging_lcoe charges the ATB increment against, zero DOF. THIS ISO'S OWN VERDICT IS MEASURED (below), so the letter is K on this ISO's own evidence. capx D50 (2026-09-04), FINDING-capx-d50-2026-09-04.md §4 -- MEASURED, DEFAULT-OFF, NOT ARMED: the t1f A/B arm neiso-t1f-d50-ccscapex (neiso-2026-2030-d50-ccscapex, key 18515067bf4d2fbe, pre-declared and matched; 6.7 min / 3.5 GB, paired with ERCOT) against the bare neiso-t1f control (neiso-2026-2030-d46-remeasure, 6690e4d6d66bc819) -- a one-field A/B. RESULT: under RGGI (29.83 / 31.92 / 34.15 $/t) the 3 GW/yr cap STILL BINDS in every year, as pre-declared (PREDECL-capx-d50 §2.3 P5): 2028 15 rows / 2,982.2 MW, 2029 12 / 2,996.7, 2030 12 / 2,982.6 (8,961.5 MW vs the control's 17 / 2,999.6 + 23 / 2,994.4 + 10 / 2,948.6 = 8,942.6); every per-year delta (-17.4 / +2.3 / +34.0 MW) within one cap-packing unit, STOP not met. The avoided-carbon leg is per tonne too, so a per-tonne island cannot unbind the cap (census: 96 % of the 12.89 GW eligible fleet clears the scaled ceiling). WHAT MOVES IS WHO CONVERTS: the control's five CC_CHP rows (139.6 / 226.8 / 8.4 MW) are gone (seam 2) and the 2028 set re-ranks toward efficient hosts, MW-weighted CO2 rate 0.608 -> 0.550 (P6 HIT -- the docstring's efficient-hosts-win ordering restored where D49 §1.4 had it inverted); 2029-2030 draw from the residual pool and drift the other way (0.429 -> 0.431, 0.361 -> 0.393; P6 MISS, recorded). Fleet MW by fuel within 20 MW, retirements / builds / backstop / reserve margin identical; generation shifts toward the converted set (gas_cc_ccs 18.27 -> 19.23 TWh in 2030); CO2 2030 14.71 -> 14.98 Mt. All 14 invariants PASS and every FC-2 row PASS on both; FC-7 PASS with the ledger built from the arm's own run_config.json (8 entries, 0 UNIDENTIFIED via the field's curated design-decision row); PROMOTE -> PROMOTE. O stays O: the owner decides. Backcast lane n/a." },
